## QUIT

Exits IBrowse.

Syntax: QUIT [FORCE/S]

Parameters:
  FORCE/S    Skip confirmation dialog

Example:
  'QUIT FORCE'

## SHOW

Restores IBrowse from iconified state and brings it to the front.

Syntax: SHOW

Alias: ACTIVATE

Example:
  'SHOW'

## ACTIVATE

Restores IBrowse from iconified state and brings it to the front.

Syntax: ACTIVATE

Alias: SHOW

Example:
  'ACTIVATE'

## HIDE

Iconifies IBrowse.

Syntax: HIDE

Alias: DEACTIVATE

Example:
  'HIDE'

## DEACTIVATE

Iconifies IBrowse.

Syntax: DEACTIVATE

Alias: HIDE

Example:
  'DEACTIVATE'

## INFO

Returns program information.

Syntax: INFO ITEM/A

Parameters:
  ITEM/A     Information to retrieve (required)
             Allowed values: TITLE, AUTHOR, COPYRIGHT, DESCRIPTION,
             VERSION, BASE, SCREEN

Return: RESULT contains the requested information
RC = -5 if ITEM is unknown.

Example:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'INFO ITEM=TITLE'
  SAY RESULT

  'INFO ITEM=VERSION'
  SAY RESULT

## HELP

Writes a list of all available ARexx commands to a file.

Syntax: HELP FILE/A

Parameters:
  FILE/A     Output file path (required)

Example:
  'HELP FILE=RAM:ibrowse_arexx.txt'

## GOTOURL

Loads a URL in the browser.

Syntax: GOTOURL URL/A [BROWSERNR/N] [SAVE/S] [RELOAD/S] [MIME]

Parameters:
  URL/A          The URL to load (required)
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)
  SAVE/S         Download file to disk instead of displaying
  RELOAD/S       Bypass cache and reload from server
  MIME           Override MIME type manually

Return: RC = -6 if no browser is active.

Examples:
  'GOTOURL "http://www.amiga.org" BROWSERNR=1'

  /* Download a file */
  'GOTOURL "http://example.com/file.lha" SAVE'

  /* Open URL in new window if no browser active */
  'GOTOURL "http://www.amiga.org"'
  IF RC ~= 0 THEN 'NEWWINDOW "http://www.amiga.org"'

## BACK

Navigates back in browser history.

Syntax: BACK [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Example:
  'BACK'
  'BACK BROWSERNR=2'

## FORWARD

Navigates forward in browser history.

Syntax: FORWARD [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Example:
  'FORWARD'
  'FORWARD BROWSERNR=2'

## HOME

Loads the homepage (as configured in IBrowse settings).

Syntax: HOME [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Example:
  'HOME'
  'HOME BROWSERNR=1'

## STOP

Stops the current loading operation.

Syntax: STOP [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Example:
  'STOP'
  'STOP BROWSERNR=3'

## RELOAD

Reloads the current page.

Syntax: RELOAD [BROWSERNR/N] [ALL/S] [FRAMES/S] [IMAGES/S]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)
  ALL/S          Reload everything (page, frames, images)
  FRAMES/S       Reload frames only
  IMAGES/S       Reload images only

Example:
  'RELOAD'
  'RELOAD ALL'
  'RELOAD IMAGES BROWSERNR=2'

## LOADIMAGES

Loads images that have not been loaded yet (e.g. when image loading is disabled).

Syntax: LOADIMAGES [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Example:
  'LOADIMAGES'
  'LOADIMAGES BROWSERNR=1'

## NEW

Opens a new window or browser (depending on IBrowse settings).

Syntax: NEW [URL]

Parameters:
  URL    URL to load in the new window/browser

Return: RESULT contains the number of the new browser/window.

Example:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'NEW'
  SAY "New browser:" RESULT

  'NEW "http://www.amiga.org"'

## NEWWINDOW

Opens a new window explicitly (always creates a new window, regardless of settings).

Syntax: NEWWINDOW [URL]

Parameters:
  URL    URL to load in the new window

Return: RESULT contains the new window number.

Example:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'NEWWINDOW "http://www.amiga.org"'
  SAY "Window:" RESULT

## NEWBROWSER

Opens a new browser tab in an existing window.

Syntax: NEWBROWSER [URL] [BROWSEWINDOWNR/N]

Parameters:
  URL                URL to load in the new browser
  BROWSEWINDOWNR/N   Target window number (default: active window)

Return: RESULT contains the new browser number.
RC = -6 if window number is invalid.

Example:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'NEWBROWSER "http://www.amiga.org"'
  SAY "Browser:" RESULT

  'NEWBROWSER "http://www.example.com" BROWSEWINDOWNR=1'

## CLOSEBROWSER

Closes a browser.

Syntax: CLOSEBROWSER [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Browser to close (default: active browser)

Example:
  'CLOSEBROWSER'
  'CLOSEBROWSER BROWSERNR=3'

## SCREENTOFRONT

Brings the IBrowse screen to the front.

Syntax: SCREENTOFRONT

Example:
  'SCREENTOFRONT'

## SCREENTOBACK

Sends the IBrowse screen to the back.

Syntax: SCREENTOBACK

Example:
  'SCREENTOBACK'

## QUERY

Queries information about a browser.

Syntax: QUERY ITEM/A [BROWSERNR/N]

Parameters:
  ITEM/A         Information to retrieve (required)
                 Allowed values: URL, TITLE, ACTIVEBROWSERNR, ACTIVEWINDOWNR
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)

Return: RESULT contains the requested information.
RC = -5 if ITEM is unknown, RC = -6 if no browser is active.

Note: ACTIVEBROWSERNR and ACTIVEWINDOWNR ignore the BROWSERNR parameter.

Examples:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'QUERY ITEM=URL BROWSERNR=2'
  SAY "URL:" RESULT

  'QUERY ITEM=TITLE'
  SAY "Title:" RESULT

  'QUERY ITEM=ACTIVEBROWSERNR'
  SAY "Active browser:" RESULT

  /* List all open URLs */
  DO i = 1 TO 20
      'QUERY ITEM=URL BROWSERNR='i
      IF RC = 0 THEN SAY 'Browser' i': ' RESULT
  END

## ADDHOTLIST

Adds an entry to the Hotlist Manager (bookmarks).

Syntax: ADDHOTLIST [GROUP/S] TITLE/A [URL] [SHORTCUT] [SHOWINMENU/N] [INSERTGROUP] [ACTIVATE/S]

Parameters:
  GROUP/S        Create a group instead of a bookmark
  TITLE/A        Name of the entry (required)
  URL            URL for the bookmark (not needed for groups)
  SHORTCUT       Keyboard shortcut for the entry
  SHOWINMENU/N   0=not shown in menu, >0=show in menu
  INSERTGROUP    Target group name (case insensitive)
  ACTIVATE/S     Open the Hotlist Manager and show the entry

Examples:
  'ADDHOTLIST TITLE="Amiga News" URL="http://www.amiga.org" INSERTGROUP="Amiga"'

  /* Create a new group */
  'ADDHOTLIST GROUP TITLE="My Links"'

  /* Add with shortcut and menu visibility */
  'ADDHOTLIST TITLE="Search" URL="http://www.google.com" SHORTCUT="g" SHOWINMENU=1'

## ADDFASTLINK

Adds a fastlink button to the toolbar.

Syntax: ADDFASTLINK TITLE/A [URL] [PROMPTTITLE/S]

Parameters:
  TITLE/A          Button title (required)
  URL              URL for the button
  PROMPTTITLE/S    Show input dialog for title

Example:
  'ADDFASTLINK TITLE="Aminet" URL="http://aminet.net"'

## OPENHOTLIST

Opens or closes the Hotlist Manager window.

Syntax: OPENHOTLIST [CLOSE/S]

Parameters:
  CLOSE/S    Close the Hotlist Manager instead of opening it

Example:
  'OPENHOTLIST'
  'OPENHOTLIST CLOSE'

## OPENHISTORY

Opens or closes the browser history window.

Syntax: OPENHISTORY [BROWSERNR/N] [CLOSE/S]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N    Target browser ID (default: active browser)
  CLOSE/S        Close the history window instead of opening it

Example:
  'OPENHISTORY'
  'OPENHISTORY BROWSERNR=2'
  'OPENHISTORY CLOSE'

## OPENCACHEBROWSER

Opens or closes the cache explorer window.

Syntax: OPENCACHEBROWSER [CLOSE/S]

Parameters:
  CLOSE/S    Close the cache explorer instead of opening it

Example:
  'OPENCACHEBROWSER'
  'OPENCACHEBROWSER CLOSE'

## OPENINFOWINDOW

Opens or closes the info window.

Syntax: OPENINFOWINDOW [CLOSE/S]

Parameters:
  CLOSE/S    Close the info window instead of opening it

Example:
  'OPENINFOWINDOW'
  'OPENINFOWINDOW CLOSE'

## FLUSH

Frees memory by clearing history, images, or cache.

Syntax: FLUSH [BROWSERNR/N] [HISTORY/S] [ALLIMAGES/S] [CACHEDIMAGES/S] [IMAGES/S]

Parameters:
  BROWSERNR/N      Target browser ID (only for HISTORY and IMAGES)
  HISTORY/S        Clear browser history
  ALLIMAGES/S      Remove all images from memory (ignores BROWSERNR)
  CACHEDIMAGES/S   Remove cached images from memory (ignores BROWSERNR)
  IMAGES/S         Remove images of the specified browser

Note: ALLIMAGES and CACHEDIMAGES affect all browsers regardless of BROWSERNR.

Examples:
  'FLUSH HISTORY BROWSERNR=2'
  'FLUSH ALLIMAGES'
  'FLUSH CACHEDIMAGES'
  'FLUSH IMAGES BROWSERNR=1'
